   "label": "The plan",
   "text": "a draft horse kicks hard (+6, 1d4+4) and has 15 HP, but it's a spooked animal, not a guard. Asleep, it can be walked past, and a bypassed monster still gives its XP."
  },
  {
   "label": "The dice",
   "text": "it shook off the first Sleep on its second save and the second outright. When it charged, the rubble held it 3 sq short. The third Sleep came up a natural 20, so he doubled its duration to 2 minutes, and the horse failed both saves."
  },
  {
   "label": "Result",
   "text": "20/20 HP, nothing lost. XP 1,000 → 1,050. No coins: there was no time to search the room before the horse woke, and a sleeping horse drops nothing."
  }
